Additionally, I might also assert that the ref the child sees is literally the child's own ref function identity (i.e., that Slot did not wrap it). This can be captured: the ref callback receives `node` — we can capture the identity of the ref by having the child component record the ref prop it received… For a host element child, we can't easily inspect the ref prop after rendering, but we can use a child component with forwardRef and record the identity of the ref it receives:

